        "modelingNotes": [
          "Exact TP900 Comfort order-number candidate, independently verified by Siemens product data: https://support.industry.siemens.com/teddatasheet/?caller=SIOS&format=pdf&language=en&mlfbs=6AV2124-0JC01-0AX0. The abbreviated TP900 family name does not establish this variant.",
          "X80.1=+24 V DC and X80.2=return; separate functional earth. Supply 19.2-28.8 V DC, 0.75 A nominal and 1.05 A maximum load-dependent; nominal power 18 W. Range/inrush/installation conditions are not inferred from the nominal schema rating.",
          "X1 has two 10/100 Mbps RJ45 sockets with integrated switch and one IP address; normalized keys X1.P1/P2 distinguish the sockets. No X3 gigabit connector exists on the 9-inch model.",
          "Optional X2 serial/PROFIBUS, X61/X62 USB-A, X60 Mini-B and X90 audio pins are independently inventoried. X2 pin purpose depends on selected RS422/485 mode; the model does not validate that configuration.",
          "Ethernet shields, connector shells, storage-card contacts and internal circuitry are not modeled as electrical terminals. No functional-earth, signal-ground, USB-ground or floating-supply commoning is inferred.",
          "Manufacturer no-connection positions remain visible as annotations; a do-not-wire policy is not enforced. Optional interface pins carry no modeled behavior; supply is the only load function."
        ]
      },
